When transitioning from a SQL background to MongoDB, the $lookup operation in an aggregation pipeline resembles a LEFT OUTER JOIN. For instance, the following MongoDB query: $lookup: { from: "xxb", localField: "xxa1", foreignField: "xxb1", as: "xxb" }
is often compared to the following SQL statement SELECT * FROM xxa LEFT JOIN xxb ON xxa.xxa1 = xxb.xxb1;
If you assume that these two operations are identical across various databases, you may misinterpret the expected outcomes and their performance: In MongoDB, any field can be a scalar or an array. The $lookup function operates as an intersection of two sets, unlike SQL's equality operator (=) which operates on two values. It is more simi…

After understanding the Playwright Test Runner and its configuration in Day 2, Day 3 is all about writing effective tests using Playwright’s powerful API. Whether you’re validating elements, simulating user flows, or verifying data, knowing the core syntax is key to writing readable and robust tests.
Test Structure and Basic Syntax
ts
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';
test('basic test example', async ({ page }) => {
https://example.com');
Key Components:
expect(): Assertion library for validations.
page: The main browser tab/context used in tests.
Commonly Used Playwright Functions
1. Navigating and Waiting
await page.goto('https://example.com');
2. Interacting with Elements
await page.click('text=Login');
3. Assertions with expect()
await expect(page).toHaveURL(/dashboard/);
Working with Locators
ts
const loginButton = page.locator('button:has-text("Login")');
Locator Tips:
Prefer text-based or role-based selectors for clarity.
page.getByRole(), page.getByLabel(), and page.getByText() are also supported.
Handling Multiple Elements
const items = page.locator('.list-item');
Form Handling Example
test('User can register', async ({ page }) => {
test@example.com');
Uploading Files
await page.setInputFiles('input[type="file"]', 'tests/files/sample.pdf');
Keyboard and Mouse Actions
await page.keyboard.type('Hello World');
Handling Alerts and Dialogs
page.on('dialog', async dialog => {
Screenshots and Video
ts
await page.screenshot({ path: 'screenshots/home.png' });
Timeouts and Retry Logic
ts
await page.waitForSelector('.loading', { timeout: 5000 });
Using Tags and Annotations
test.skip('feature not ready', async ({ page }) => { ... });
test.describe('Checkout Flow', () => {
Summary
Write expressive and maintainable test cases
Interact with modern, dynamic UIs easily
Validate web application behavior precisely
Improve debugging with locators, traces, and reports
